# CODEOWNERS — required reviewers for changes that reach the cluster or cloud.
#
# POLICY (owner ruling, 2026-10-05): bot-approved ships. The gate set — the full
# CI matrix plus gate-* (ds-conformance, frames-first, authz, identifier, …) — is
# the production guard. Once those gates pass and the PR is bot-approved,
# ordinary code ships without a human in the loop. This matches the hardening
# model in governance/hardening-convention.md §6 ("a bot-authored, bot-approved
# PR that clears every gate ships to prod — this is deliberate").
#
# Code-owner review therefore does NOT apply to ordinary code. There is no
# catch-all owner here: a `* @izzywdev` entry made every change wait on a human,
# which contradicted the bot-approved-ships model and silently stalled otherwise
# green, gate-passing PRs. It was removed deliberately — do not reinstate it.
#
# Code-owner review is reserved for the DEPLOY + GOVERNANCE surface, where the
# merge approval IS the deploy/apply/policy approval and a bad change bypasses the
# gates above:
#   - deploy/terraform/** : out-of-cluster IaC, applied by FuzeInfra (Cloudflare,
#     nodes, cloud). A bad change here can alter prod infrastructure.
#   - deploy/argocd/**    : Argo Applications (pull-reconciled onto the cluster).
#   - deploy/helm/**      : the prod chart + values-prod (image tags, ingress) that
#     Argo deploys — changes here ship to prod.
#   - .github/workflows/** : CI/CD incl. the infra-dispatch + release pipelines,
#     and the gate workflows that ARE the production guard.
#   - .github/CODEOWNERS   : this review policy itself stays owner-gated, so the
#     guard surface can't be narrowed on a bot approval.
# The "Protect Master" ruleset keeps require_code_owner_review: true; with no
# catch-all it now bites only on the paths below.

/deploy/terraform/    @izzywdev
/deploy/argocd/       @izzywdev
/deploy/helm/         @izzywdev
/.github/workflows/   @izzywdev
/.github/CODEOWNERS   @izzywdev
